node_modules/
*.astraplugin
# …except the vendored cross-repo test vectors. They are frozen bytes with
# their expected verdicts and digests recorded beside them, vendored from
# AstraPlugins/testdata/bundles by tools/vendor-testdata.sh there. Without this
# line the selftest's shared-vector half has no fixtures in a fresh checkout.
!tests/vectors/*.astraplugin
.DS_Store

# ── private key material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defence in depth, not the primary control. The primary control is that
# tools/keygen-root.sh refuses to run inside a git work tree at all and writes
# the ceremony directory under $HOME by default; the index signing key never
# touches a file, only $ASTRA_INDEX_SIGNING_KEY in the `publish` environment.
# This is here for the one path neither of those covers: a human copying a key
# in to look at it, and then running `git add -A`.
#
# `*.private.pem` is the exact name keygen-root.sh writes. The broader patterns
# are for anything a hand or another tool produces.
*.pem
*.key
*.private.*
# …except the TEST keys, which are committed ON PURPOSE. Their private halves
# are published so the daemon's unit tests and astra-registry's selftest can
# sign fixtures with the same keys, and both repositories derive them from seed
# phrases printed in tools/testkeys/README.md. They are named so that no one
# could mistake them for production material, and the daemon can only compile
# them in behind a non-default feature that a release profile refuses.
!tools/testkeys/*.SECRET-TEST-KEY.json

# Installers are 87 MB and belong on the CDN, never in this history. A stray
# `git add -A` with one of these present is permanent, and this repository is
# public. Test fixtures for the signer go in tools/testkeys/fixtures/ instead.
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg
